{"uid":"src/box_style.c::bx_replaced_box","name":"bx_replaced_box","qualname":"bx_replaced_box","kind":"function","file":"src/box_style.c","line":319,"end_line":331,"language":"c","signature":"int bx_replaced_box(int w_px, int w_pct, int aspect_num, int aspect_den, double avail_w, double *out_w, double *out_h)","params":[{"name":"w_px","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"w_pct","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"aspect_num","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"aspect_den","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"avail_w","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"out_w","annotation":"double *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"out_h","annotation":"double *","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"int","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"The used BOX of a replaced element (image/video) that has no intrinsic pixel size of its own -- because it did not load, or was never allowed to.","description":"CSS Sizing 4 section 4: when one axis is definite and an aspect-ratio is present,\nthe ratio supplies the other. That is what makes a blocked thumbnail keep the\nshape the author reserved for it instead of collapsing to a text-height bar and\nletting its `alt` reflow the page. Freedom renders this case by default (images\noff; third-party images blocked even when on), so it is the common path, not an\nedge case.\n\nw_px / w_pct are the declared width's two halves (CSS_LEN_UNSET / 0 for absent),\nresolved against avail_w exactly like every other <length-percentage>.\naspect_num / aspect_den are the ratio x1000 (0 = none).\n\nReturns 1 and writes *out_w / *out_h only when BOTH a positive used width and a\nusable ratio are available; otherwise returns 0 and touches nothing, leaving the\ncaller's own fallback in place rather than inventing a height. Pure.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[["Inherited","Documentation from `bx_replaced_box` (include/box_style.h:196)."]],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"src/box_style.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":["src/box_style.c::bx_width_cap"],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"src/box_style.c::bx_border_box_h","name":"bx_border_box_h","qualname":"bx_border_box_h","kind":"function","file":"src/box_style.c","line":333,"end_line":342,"language":"c","signature":"double bx_border_box_h(double declared_h, int border_box, double pad_t, double pad_b, double bord_t, double bord_b)","params":[{"name":"declared_h","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"border_box","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"pad_t","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"pad_b","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"bord_t","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"bord_b","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"double","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Border-box height for a DECLARED height under box-sizing (CSS 2.1 10.6.3, CSS Box Sizing 3 section 4).","description":"With content-box -- the CSS default, so the common case -- `height` sizes the CONTENT, and the vertical padding and border sit OUTSIDE it: a `height:60px; padding:2%` box is taller than 60px. With border-box the declared height already includes them and this is the identity. Negative edges are treated as 0; the result is never negative.\n\nThe horizontal twin is bx_content_cap, which converts the other way (a\ndeclared border-box WIDTH into the content width cap) because widths are\ncapped and heights are set. Pure.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[["Inherited","Documentation from `bx_border_box_h` (include/box_style.h:210)."]],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"src/box_style.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"src/box_style.c::bx_content_clipped","name":"bx_content_clipped","qualname":"bx_content_clipped","kind":"function","file":"src/box_style.c","line":344,"end_line":348,"language":"c","signature":"int bx_content_clipped(int overflow_x, int overflow_y)","params":[{"name":"overflow_x","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"overflow_y","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"int","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"","description":"","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"src/box_style.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"src/box_style.c::bx_lp_px","name":"bx_lp_px","qualname":"bx_lp_px","kind":"function","file":"src/box_style.c","line":350,"end_line":359,"language":"c","signature":"double bx_lp_px(int px_val, int pct_pm, double basis)","params":[{"name":"px_val","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"pct_pm","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"basis","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"double","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Used px value of a <length-percentage> (CSS Values 4 section 5.3): the px half plus pct_pm per-mille of `basis`.","description":"This is the ONLY place the engine turns a percentage into pixels, and the rule is the whole of it -- there is no clamping, no minimum and no special case here, because none of those are properties of the value type.\n\n`basis` is the containing-block dimension the property resolves against.\nWhich dimension that is belongs to the caller and is NOT symmetric: CSS 2.1\nsections 8.3/8.4 resolve ALL FOUR margin and padding percentages against the\ncontaining block WIDTH, padding-top and padding-bottom included. The full\nproperty -> basis table is spec/css_length.md section 7.3.\n\npx_val may carry a CSS_LEN_UNSET/CSS_LEN_AUTO sentinel, which contributes 0\n(a percentage-only value states no absolute length). A basis that is not a\nusable length contributes nothing while the absolute half survives. Pure.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[["Inherited","Documentation from `bx_lp_px` (include/box_style.h:236)."]],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"src/box_style.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":["src/box_style.c::bx_background_layer","src/box_style.c::bx_width_cap"]}
{"uid":"src/box_style.c::bx_content_cap","name":"bx_content_cap","qualname":"bx_content_cap","kind":"function","file":"src/box_style.c","line":361,"end_line":370,"language":"c","signature":"double bx_content_cap(double width_cap, int border_box, double pad_l, double pad_r, double bord_l, double bord_r)","params":[{"name":"width_cap","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"border_box","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"pad_l","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"pad_r","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"bord_l","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"bord_r","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"double","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Content-width cap adjusted for box-sizing (2026-07-11).","description":"With border_box set, the declared width includes the horizontal padding and border, so the cap on the CONTENT is width_cap minus those edges, clamped >= 1 (a border-box narrower than its own edges never yields a negative width). border_box == 0 (content-box or unset) or width_cap <= 0 (no cap) are the identity. Negative edges are treated as 0. Pure.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[["Inherited","Documentation from `bx_content_cap` (include/box_style.h:244)."]],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"src/box_style.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
